  "expect": {
    "volume": 16727.65486704782,
    "faces": 9,
    "bbox": [
      0,
      -10,
      0,
      60,
      10,
      20
    ],
    "source": "analytic",
    "note": "Wedge: XZ profile (0,0)-(60,0)-(60,20)-(0,10), 20 wide: V = 900*20 = 18000; its top is the plane z = 10 + x/6. Adjust: every hole (r 3 at x = 10, 30, 50) is cut from z = 0 up to the slope where it lands, so each goes through the part: removed = pi*9*(z(10) + z(30) + z(50)) = pi*9*(35/3 + 15 + 55/3) = 405 pi (a cylinder cut by a slanted plane holds its area times the height at its centre). V = 18000 - 405 pi. Faces: the wedge's 6 + 3 hole walls = 9."
  }
